cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Experimentally mapped aggregation-critical protein regions, with circularity and prediction-concordance labels"
abstract: >-
  A hand-curated set of protein regions shown experimentally to be required for,
  or to constitute the core of, protein aggregation. Every row was established by
  opening the source paper and checking the claim against it. Each region carries
  the construct that established it, whether a predictor was in its discovery
  path (circularity), and whether experiment and prediction agree (stratum).
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Mercier des Rochettes"
    given-names: "Bertrand"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1145-1881"
    email: "contact@quantum-proteins.ai"
    affiliation: "Quantum Proteins AI, Cergy-Pontoise, France"
# Co-authors: NONE. Settled by the author 16 Nov 2026, asked and answered rather
# than assumed. Sole authorship is deliberate, not an oversight.
keywords:
  - protein aggregation
  - amyloid
  - benchmark dataset
  - aggregation prediction
  - circularity
  - curated dataset
# DECIDED by the author, 16 Nov 2026. Full legal code is in LICENSE.
# CC-BY-4.0 over CC0 because the value of this dataset is curatorial: the
# provenance, the circularity calls and the stratum labels are the work, and
# attribution is what makes a reader go back and check them. CC0 would maximise
# reuse but detach the rows from the reasoning that justifies them.
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/quantumproteinsai/mentalillness"
date-released: 2026-11-16
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24290698"  # reserved on Zenodo 16 Nov 2026, registered at publication
